+/-- Static label of a nondeterministic choice (an `undefined_*` / `internal_pick` call site).
+The Sail-to-Lean backend emits one label per call site, so a labelled draw reads the oracle
+without advancing any state: two control-flow paths that perform different draws still end in
+the same state, which lets a specializer merge them.
+* `site n`    : call site `n`, statically checked to execute at most once per top-level call.
+* `occ n k`   : `k`-th dynamic execution of call site `n` (sites that may execute repeatedly:
+                inside loops, recursive functions, or helpers invoked more than once).
+* `child ℓ i` : `i`-th draw inside a generated `undefined_<T>` initialiser called with label `ℓ`.
+* `anon k`    : `k`-th unlabelled draw (legacy `choose`; hand-written code only). -/
+inductive ChoiceLabel where
+  | site (n : Nat)
+  | occ (n k : Nat)
